⚡️🇱🇧 The Central Criminal Investigations surrounded all entrances of Bhannes Hospital and arrested Riad Salameh.

Riad Salameh is the former governor of Lebanon's Central Bank (Banque du Liban), serving from 1993 to 2023. He is responsible for managing the financial policies that led to Lebanon's 2019 economic collapse, and was arrested on charges of embezzling tens of millions of dollars in public funds, money laundering, and financial fraud.

